    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.colors\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.12 (!at least latest Nightly build!)\n\n### Description\n\nChanging the colorscheme using `Pick colorschemes` more than once with `vim._core.ui2` enabled causes the following error:\n\n```\nE5108: Lua: ...re/nvim/site/pack/core/opt/mini.nvim/lua/mini/colors.lua:1668: Invalid highlight name: 'SpecialKeyxxx'\nstack traceback:\n\t[C]: in function 'nvim_get_hl_by_name'\n\t...re/nvim/site/pack/core/opt/mini.nvim/lua/mini/colors.lua:1668: in function 'get_hl_by_name'\n\t...re/nvim/site/pack/core/opt/mini.nvim/lua/mini/colors.lua:1661: in function 'get_current_groups'\n\t...re/nvim/site/pack/core/opt/mini.nvim/lua/mini/colors.lua:776: in function 'get_colorscheme'\n\t...are/nvim/site/pack/core/opt/mini.nvim/lua/mini/extra.lua:410: in function 'colorschemes'\n\t/home/clover/.config/nvim/plugin/30_mini_pick+visits.lua:591: in function </home/clover/.config/nvim/plugin/30_mini_pick+visits.lua:591>\n```\n\nIt seems that two strings are being unintentionally concatenated somewhere in the output. From the `:highlight` output:\n\n```\nSpecialKey     xxx links to Special\n```\n\nIt's most likely a Neovim issue, but it would be great if you could take a closer look. Thanks 🙂\n\n### Reproduction\n\n```lua\nrequire(\"vim._core.ui2\").enable({})\n\nvim.pack.add({\n  { src = \"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim\", version = \"main\" },\n})\n\nrequire(\"mini.pick\").setup()\nrequire(\"mini.extra\").setup()\n\nvim.keymap.set(\"n\", \"<Leader>fc\", \":Pick colorschemes<CR>\")\n```\n\n```\nnvim --noplugin -u repro.lua repro.lua\n\\fc + choose\n\\fc + choose -> Error\n```",
