        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Yes indeed, this is a Neovim upstream issue. It manifests itself here due to [how 'mini.colors' computes all available highlight groups](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/577d2dcb558efce1518c45a76345e01bf346c8e8/lua/mini/colors.lua#L1652) (granted, it is a bit outdated, but still).\n\nIt can be reproduced without 'mini.nvim':\n\n1. `nvim --clean`\n2. `:lua require('vim._core.ui2').enable({})`\n3. `:=vim.api.nvim_exec2('highlight', { output = true }).output`. The first \"line\" is as expected: `SpecialKey     xxx links to Special`\n4. `:=vim.api.nvim_exec2('highlight', { output = true }).output` again. The first \"line\" is not as expected: `SpecialKeyxxx links to Special`\n\nClosing as an upstream Neovim issue. Although could be remedied by refactoring 'mini.colors'.",
